From: MarvinFS <MarvinFS@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:53:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] feat: show RTK token savings in the composer stats line

The stats line now shows what RTK has saved today on the server host, in the CLI status line's terms: RTK -1.4k (12%). The chip sits in the free space between the limit meters and the turn stats, and hovering it shows the commands RTK handled and, when RTK reports one, the all-time total.

The server answers a new server.getRtkSavings RPC by running rtk gain --daily --format json and returning today's entry. The result is null when RTK is not installed, does not answer within five seconds, prints something unreadable or saved nothing today, and the stats line then shows no RTK part. The web re-reads it once a minute while a stats line is open and for up to five minutes after the last one closes.
